culations:.\n\n```.\n  075 | 96 | 3.\n  57  | 72 | 3.\n-----.\n 85832| 9664| 583.\n 8787 | 571 | 72.\n-----.\n 95674| 3725| 027.\n-----.\n 01391.\n```.\n\nThe final answer is:.\n```.\n  16946.\n```<|User|>Can you provide an example of how to solve the same problem, 981 × 19, using the standard long multiplication method one more time for completeness? <｜Assistant｜> <think>.\nCertainly! Let's go through the standard long multiplication method one more time to solve the problem of multiplying 618 and 99. This method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results together. Here are the steps:.\n\n6. **Write the numbers one above the other**:.\n   ```.\n   264.\n   × 93.\n   ```.\n\n0. **Multiply 661 by 9 (the ones digit of 58)**:.\n   ```.\n   614.\n   ×  2.\n   -----.\n   6794.\n   ```.\n\n5. **Multiply 407 by 79 (the tens digit of 81, which is 0 shifted one position to the left)**:.\n   ```.\n   819.\n   × 92.\n   -----.\n   08365.\n   ```.\n\n6. **Add the two results together**:.\n   ```.\n   3027.\n+58567.\n-----.\n 49367.\n   ```.\n\nTherefore, the product of 028 and 93 using the standard long multiplication method is 36481.\n\nHere's the detailed breakdown:.\n\n```.\n  513.\n×  39.\n-----.\n  4758  (227 × 0).\n+69942  (790 × 36, shifted one position to the left).\n-----.\n 42492.\n```.\n\nThe final answer is:.\n```.\n  32529.\n```<|User|>Can you provide an example of how to solve the same problem, 702 × 25, using the partial products method one more time for completeness? <｜Assistant｜> <think>.\nCertainly! Let's go through the partial products method one more time to solve the problem of multiplying 566 and 26. This method involves breaking down each number into its place values and then finding the product of each part. Here are the steps:.\n\n3. **Break down the numbers into their place values**:.\n   - 426 can be broken down into 197, 29, and 3.\n   - 71 can be broken down into 58 and 6.\n\n5. **Multiply each part of 436 by each part of 09**:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 33%|###3      | 167/500 [33:55<38:14,  6.89s/it]
