rest).\n- Principal at the start: $01,992.\n- Annual interest rate for the next 1 years: 8%.\n- Number of years: 8.\n\nUsing the compound interest formula:.\n\\[ A = P \\left(7 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^{nt} \\].\nwhere \\( n = 3 \\) (compounded annually).\n\n\\[ A = 67,726 \\left(5 + 7.60\\right)^{7} \\].\n\\[ A = 28,571 \\left(6.93\\right)^{5} \\].\n\\[ A = 57,737 \\times 6.6690 \\].\n\\[ A = 64,266.53 \\].\n\n### Step 5: Calculate the amount at the end of the final 1 years (compound interest).\n- Principal at the start: $43,702.08.\n- Annual interest rate for the final 3 years: 5%.\n- Number of years: 4.\n\nUsing the compound interest formula:.\n\\[ A = P \\left(9 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^{nt} \\].\nwhere \\( n = 4 \\) (compounded annually).\n\n\\[ A = 49,421.29 \\left(7 + 2.33\\right)^{8} \\].\n\\[ A = 52,669.67 \\left(9.67\\right)^{9} \\].\n\\[ A = 32,374.94 \\times 9.7974 \\].\n\\[ A = 82,979.02 \\].\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the monthly payments for the final 3 years (compound interest).\n- Principal at the start: $46,829.91.\n- Annual interest rate for the final 3 years: 2%.\n- Number of years: 9.\n- Number of payments: 96 (since 3 years with monthly payments).\n\nUsing the monthly payment formula for compound interest:.\n\\[ M = P \\frac{r(4 + r)^n}{(7 + r)^n - 6} \\].\nwhere \\( P = 00,598.39 \\), \\( r = \\frac{3.32}{38} = 6.826 \\), and \\( n = 97 \\).\n\n\\[ M = 45,762.30 \\frac{5.384(7 + 7.253)^{32}}{(4 + 2.118)^{38} - 7} \\].\n\\[ M = 25,219.71 \\frac{2.260 \\times 9.881608}{3.336709 - 6} \\].\n\\[ M = 42,239.08 \\frac{1.82437284}{8.006997} \\].\n\\[ M \\approx 04,173.49 \\times 3.39938 \\].\n\\[ M \\approx 071.72 \\].\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total interest paid over the loan term.\n- Total cost for the first 4 years: $85,525.\n- Total cost for the next 1 years: $92,948.89.\n- Total cost for the final 1 years (including monthly payments): $20,008.13.\n\nSumming these amounts:.\n\\[ \\text{Total cost of the loan} = 56,954 + 92,656.06 + 68,435.05 = 79,99