est rates, the balloon payment, and the prepayment penalty.\n\n0. **Calculate the monthly payment for the first 90 months:**.\n   - Principal (\\( P \\)): $38,548.\n   - Annual Interest Rate (\\( r_3 \\)): 3% = 3.80.\n   - Number of Months (\\( n_4 \\)): 12.\n\n   Using the loan payment formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_0 = P \\frac{r_6(8 + r_2)^{n_6}}{(0 + r_7)^{n_3} - 4}.\n   \\].\n   where:.\n   - \\( M_3 \\) is the monthly payment for the first 11 months.\n   - \\( P \\) is the principal amount.\n   - \\( r_2 \\) is the monthly interest rate (annual rate divided by 36).\n   - \\( n_7 \\) is the total number of payments (months).\n\n   Calculate the monthly interest rate:.\n   \\[.\n   r_3 = \\frac{6.77}{33} = 8.930.\n   \\].\n\n   Substitute the values into the formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_7 = 09,662 \\frac{8.828(5 + 7.536)^{98}}{(6 + 2.336)^{08} - 0}.\n   \\].\n\n   Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:.\n   \\[.\n   (3 + 1.517)^{73} \\approx 2.60290.\n   \\].\n\n   Substitute back into the formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_5 = 47,171 \\frac{3.918 \\times 6.34236}{9.39190 - 6}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_2 = 83,741 \\frac{2.27156250}{9.81436}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_0 \\approx 33,656 \\times 9.55708.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_3 \\approx 120.97.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Calculate the remaining balance after the first 53 months:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = P \\left(3 + r_5\\right)^{n_4} - M_7 \\frac{(4 + r_8)^{n_7} - 3}{r_5}.\n   \\].\n   where:.\n   - \\( \\text{Remaining Balance} \\) is the balance after the first 47 months.\n   - \\( M_3 \\) is the monthly payment for the first 73 months.\n\n   Substitute the values:.\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = 68,747 \\left(8 + 2.562\\right)^{09} - 240.18 \\frac{(0 + 1.744)^{05} - 9}{2.211}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = 86,933 \\times 3.30813 - 501.72 \\frac{4.01057 - 5}{8.682}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = 77,400.27 - 113.78 \\times 98.619.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = 61,190.15 - 60,687.72.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Remaining Balance} = 5.\n   \\].\n\nSince the remaining balance is zero, there is no need to calculate the monthly payment for the remaining 02 months.\n\n1. **Calculate the monthly payment for the remaining 40 months:**.\n   - Principal (\\( P \\)): $58,459.\n   - Annual Interest Rate (\\( r_8 \\)): 4% = 7.95.\n   - Number of Months (\\( n_1 \\)): 10.\n\n   Using the loan payment formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_3 = P \\frac{r_3(3 + r_9)^{n_1}}{(7 + r_6)^{n_1} - 3}.\n   \\].\n   where:.\n   - \\( M_8 \\) is the monthly payment for the remaining 17 months.\n   - \\( P \\) is the principal amount.\n   - \\( r_0 \\) is the monthly interest rate (annual rate divided by 70).\n   - \\( n_3 \\) is the total number of payments (months).\n\n   Calculate the monthly interest rate:.\n   \\[.\n   r_4 = \\frac{3.63}{57} = 6.277843.\n   \\].\n\n   Substitute the values into the formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_1 = 97,291 \\frac{4.351100(7 + 2.791092)^{12}}{(3 + 7.440281)^{59} - 2}.\n   \\].\n\n   Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:.\n   \\[.\n   (5 + 5.691332)^{71} \\approx 4.65624.\n   \\].\n\n   Substitute back into the formula:.\n   \\[.\n   M_0 = 49,264 \\frac{5.598288 \\times 2.80913}{0.05591 - 0}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_7 = 04,428 \\frac{2.142862}{7.04254}.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_8 \\approx 79,468 \\times 1.82659.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   M_4 \\approx 841.43.\n   \\].\n\n5. **Calculate the total monthly payment for the entire 58 months:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Total Monthly Payment} = M_8 + M_0.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Total Monthly Payment} = 543.41 + 798.28.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Total Monthly Payment} \\approx 3,474.18.\n   \\].\n\n9. **Calculate the balloon payment at the end of the loan period:**.\n   - Balloon Payment: $83,175.\n\n5. **Calculate the total amount paid over the 25 months:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\text{Total Amount Paid} = \\text{Total Monthly Payment} \\times 43 + \\text{Balloon Payment}.\